  [PASS] BG-0  the CAMB smooth-dust route (dark-energy fluid carrying a tabulated w(a) = -Om_L/(Om_d a^-3+Om_L), omega_cdm -> 0) reproduces LCDM's expansion history EXACTLY: max |H_smooth/H_LCDM - 1| < 1e-7 over 0 < z < 10^6. The two models therefore have the same theta_star, the same sound horizon and the same z_eq, and any C_l difference is a PERTURBATION difference, never a background one   (max |H_s/H_L - 1| = 3.48e-09 over z = 0..1e6;  100*theta_s = 1.0411781)

